60,3,1,talk,Rin,,Option A is too chaotic for my schedule. Option B sounds like a nightmare of setup time. I prefer C.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option A and B incur recurring costs or wasted space. Option C is the most fiscally responsible.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Option C creates a permanent hierarchy of ""good"" and ""bad"" seats. Option B is fairer for the window access.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option A and B are impossible for ergonomics. I need a fixed spot to keep my settings. I vote C.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Option C helps functional work, but Option B keeps us mixing. However, the shuffle interruptions are scary.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Mizuki, can't we just rotate who gets the window in Option C every few months manually?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,That would trigger the facilities charge for power and network again.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,Then Option B is the only way to ensure equity without constant manual requests.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, the physical toll of resetting a desk every rotation is too high.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"I'm leaning toward C for stability, as long as we make an effort to talk.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm sticking with C. I need my morning to be fast.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I vote C. It's the only one that doesn't bleed money.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,I still feel B is the only fair choice for the environment. I vote B.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,I vote C. My back and my ears can't handle the alternatives.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I'll go with C. Stability prevents those long periods of chaos.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
